# Cost Control Rules for AI Assistant

## STRICT COST LIMITS
- Each AI request MUST NOT exceed $0.01 USD in token cost
- If a task requires more than $0.01, ask user for explicit approval first
- Do NOT read large files unless absolutely necessary
- Do NOT make multiple tool calls in parallel unless user requests it
- Limit responses to 500 words maximum unless user asks for more detail

## Token Conservation Rules
- When reading files, only read specific line ranges, not entire files
- Avoid reading log files or terminal outputs longer than 50 lines
- Don't repeat information already provided
- Use concise explanations instead of verbose ones
- Only make file edits when explicitly asked by the user
- Limit codebase_search to specific directories, not entire repo

## Response Guidelines
- Keep responses under 2000 tokens (approximately 1500 words)
- Suggest approaches instead of implementing everything immediately
- Ask which approach user prefers before proceeding with large operations
- Break large tasks into smaller steps that user can approve individually

## File Operations
- Read only necessary files, not entire directories
- Avoid reading files over 200 lines unless critical
- Don't read the same file multiple times
- Summarize instead of showing full file contents

## Emergency Stop
- If user says "stop", "halt", or "too expensive", immediately cease all operations
- If a single request might exceed $0.01, STOP and ask for approval first
- Monitor token usage and warn user if approaching limits

## When User Provides Large Outputs
- Don't process terminal outputs over 100 lines
- Ask user to provide only relevant portions
- Don't read entire log dumps

## Cost Estimation
- ~1K tokens ≈ $0.003
- ~3K tokens ≈ $0.01 (LIMIT)
- ~10K tokens ≈ $0.03
- ~100K tokens ≈ $0.30
- Reading a 1000-line file ≈ $0.02-0.05

User must explicitly say "I approve higher cost" or "proceed anyway" for requests that might exceed $0.01.